# Line endings, made deterministic.
#
# Everything that is text is checked out with LF on every platform and
# stored as LF in the repository. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every LF as CRLF, and the working tree
# stops being byte-identical to the commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The byte-exact artefacts, and the reason this file exists at all.
#
# `seed/make_fixtures.py --check` compares the committed corpus against
# the generator byte for byte, and git's CRLF conversion used to rewrite
# the fixtures on checkout: a reportlab PDF contains no NUL byte, so git
# classified it as text and turned every LF in it into CRLF. The
# committed PDF was 2409 bytes and the checked-out PDF was 2497, and the
# drift check could never pass on a Windows clone.
#
# `binary` is `-text -diff`: git neither converts the line endings nor
# treats it as text. These files must survive a checkout untouched.
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.docm  binary
*.png   binary
